port the refutation rather than manufacture a proof.\n\nBlocked: both target statements are false because `SlitPath` does not require `γ′/γ` to be interval-integrable or require `γ` to be absolutely continuous.\n\nA concrete counterexample is obtained from an oscillatory angle. For `t > 0`, define\n\n```text\nθ(t) = t * (2 + sin(1 / t²))\nγ(t) = π * exp(i * θ(t))\n```\n\nand set `γ(0) = π`.\n\nThis satisfies `SlitPath`:\n\n- `γ(0) = π`.\n- For `0 < t ≤ 1`, `0 < θ(t) ≤ 3 < π`, so `γ(t)` avoids the nonnegative real axis.\n- `γ` is continuous on `[0,1]`.\n- `γ` is differentiable at every `t > 0`.\n\nMoreover,\n\n```text\nγ′(t) / γ(t) = i * θ′(t)\nθ′(t) = 2 + sin(1/t²) - (2/t²) cos(1/t²).\n```\n\nThe absolute integral of `θ′` diverges near zero. Thus `γ′/γ` is not Bochner-integrable on `[0,1]`, and Mathlib’s convention gives:\n\n```text\nlogIntegral γ = 0\n```\n\nthrough `intervalIntegral.integral_undef`.\n\nHowever, the one-sided argument limit exists and equals zero, while\n\n```text\nargStar (γ 1) = θ(1) = 2 + sin 1 > 0.\n```\n\nTherefore `logIntegral_im_eq_argStar_diff` asserts:\n\n```text\n0 = 2 + sin 1\n```\n\nwhich is false. The same path refutes `logIntegral_im_bounds`, since its first conclusion becomes `0 < |0|`.\n\nThe required structural repair is one of:\n\n- add `IntervalIntegrable (fun t => deriv γ t / γ t) volume 0 1`;\n- require appropriate absolute continuity of `logStar ∘ γ`; or\n- define `logIntegral` as a convergent improper integral and include that convergence in `SlitPath`.\n\nSearch report:\n\n- Search arm (a) carried the diagnosis.\n- Queries:\n  - Loogle: `intervalIntegral integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt integrable derivative`\n  - LeanSearch: `Mathlib fundamental theorem calculus derivative integrable interval`\n  - LeanSearch: `Lean intervalIntegral integral_undef nonintegrable`\n  - Local: `integral_eq_sub_of_hasDeriv`, `integral_deriv_eq_sub`, `intervalIntegrable.*deriv`, `integral_undef`\n- Relevant declarations:\n  - `intervalIntegral.inte